$ jailops remote add <addr> --token <trust-token>
! usage: the trust token is malformed: jailops: malformed trust token
! hint: run 'jailops remote add --help' for usage
[exit 2]

$ jailops remote add <addr> --token <trust-token> --dry-run
dry-run: would redeem a trust token at https://<addr> and add remote 127-0-0-1
pinned: <fingerprint>

$ jailops remote add <addr> --token <trust-token> --name trusting
remote/trusting added: trusted as laptop (operator, web), server pinned 46:81:74:fd:18:ae:99:0a...; now the current remote
connected to trusting (version fake), seen as trusted

$ jailops whoami
User:        cert:laptop
Kind:        certificate
Role:        operator
Scope:       web
Remote:      trusting (https://<addr>)
Project:     

$ jailops whoami -o json
{
  "user": "cert:laptop",
  "kind": "certificate",
  "permission": "operator",
  "projects": [
    "web"
  ],
  "remote": "trusting",
  "project": ""
}

$ jailops remote list
    NAME       TARGET                               AUTH          HOST   SOURCE
    local      unix:/var/run/jailops/jailops.sock   root only     -      built-in
*   trusting   https://<addr>              mtls+pinned   -      user

$ jailops remote add <addr> --token <trust-token> --name again
! unauthorized: invalid trust token
! hint: Check the token with 'jailops remote list' and 'jailops doctor'; create a new token on the server if needed. (jailops explain unauthorized)
[exit 3]

$ jailops project create other
! forbidden: the operator role cannot call POST /api/v1/projects
! hint: your role or scope does not allow this: ask an administrator ('jailops whoami' shows yours)
[exit 3]

$ jailops list --project web
! No jails in project web. Create one with: jailops jail create NAME --image IMAGE --network NETWORK --storage STORAGE

$ jailops list --project default
! not_found: project "default" not found
! hint: list them with 'jailops project list'; check --project, --host and --remote too
[exit 4]

$ jailops whoami
User:        cert:laptop
Kind:        certificate
Role:        readonly
Scope:       web
Remote:      trusting (https://<addr>)
Project:     

$ jailops whoami
! unauthorized: missing or invalid token
! hint: Check the token with 'jailops remote list' and 'jailops doctor'; create a new token on the server if needed. (jailops explain unauthorized)
[exit 3]

